        <div><a name="_manchu" id="_manchu"></a><p class="h2Annex">C.30 Manchu</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_33c89cbd-9f1a-4e5b-8a2e-a107f9573878" id="_33c89cbd-9f1a-4e5b-8a2e-a107f9573878"></a>name components:</p>

  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo32;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    family name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo32;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
    given name
  </p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_069bccf8-b044-456f-a3c3-19e4f44ae73f" id="_069bccf8-b044-456f-a3c3-19e4f44ae73f"></a>Manchus are called only by their given names.
Manchu clan names (&#x201C;hala&#x201D;) are not used with their personal names,
but occasionally a family name is used.</p>
<div><a name="_typical_name_patterns_10" id="_typical_name_patterns_10"></a><p class="h3Annex">C.30.1 Typical name patterns</p><p class="TableTitle" align="center">Table C.40</p><div align="center"><table style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;" class="MsoISOTable" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><a name="_e59c269e-d514-4e40-a406-8d90ceb856b6" id="_e59c269e-d514-4e40-a406-8d90ceb856b6"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="TableTitle" align="center">Table C.41</p><div align="center"><table style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;" class="MsoISOTable" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><a name="_2748cc04-a3b4-4817-948f-dc27b65be6b7" id="_2748cc04-a3b4-4817-948f-dc27b65be6b7"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">family name</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="TableTitle" align="center">Table C.42</p><div align="center"><table style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;" class="MsoISOTable" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><a name="_f40511db-cc6f-4e00-a4a3-e9f0b6fdf857" id="_f40511db-cc6f-4e00-a4a3-e9f0b6fdf857"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">family name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>
<div><a name="_examples_10" id="_examples_10"></a><p class="h3Annex">C.30.2 Examples</p><div class="example"><a name="_142ff01e-df54-44cb-bddd-b74fc0e49de4" id="_142ff01e-df54-44cb-bddd-b74fc0e49de4"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  1</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x201C;Tuli&#x161;en&#x201D;</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_d94ab68a-0fc5-43d2-a1a0-b0532c61de48" id="_d94ab68a-0fc5-43d2-a1a0-b0532c61de48"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  2</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x201C;Hiowan Ye&#x201D; (&#x7384;&#x70E8;)</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_4422f95f-1c70-4212-9629-a02ca18ee196" id="_4422f95f-1c70-4212-9629-a02ca18ee196"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  3</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x201C;Aisin-Gioro Ulhicun&#x201D;, linguist. The family name is &#x201C;Aisin-Gioro&#x201D;.</p></div></div></div>
        <div><a name="_mongolian" id="_mongolian"></a><p class="h2Annex">C.31 Mongolian</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_5c1308bc-4bee-49eb-b175-67ec69bb8317" id="_5c1308bc-4bee-49eb-b175-67ec69bb8317"></a>name components:</p>

  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo33;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    given name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo33;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
    clan name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo33;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
    family name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo33;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
    genonymic name
  </p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_8a1d610f-3df9-48b9-a998-621b2461a61d" id="_8a1d610f-3df9-48b9-a998-621b2461a61d"></a>Mongolian names traditionally consists of only one personal name.</p>
<div><a name="_typical_name_patterns_11" id="_typical_name_patterns_11"></a><p class="h3Annex">C.31.1 Typical name patterns</p><p class="TableTitle" align="center">Table C.43</p><div align="center"><table style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;" class="MsoISOTable" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><a name="_6591b2d1-fd69-4e34-a130-6d1932946c15" id="_6591b2d1-fd69-4e34-a130-6d1932946c15"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">clan name</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="TableTitle" align="center">Table C.44</p><div align="center"><table style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;" class="MsoISOTable" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><a name="_cc13416a-e634-418c-b79a-18b648ba7692" id="_cc13416a-e634-418c-b79a-18b648ba7692"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">family name</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
