        <div><a name="_vietnamese" id="_vietnamese"></a><p class="h2Annex">C.48 Vietnamese</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_592ff2dd-76a1-426d-b2d2-ab7cb5d19f15" id="_592ff2dd-76a1-426d-b2d2-ab7cb5d19f15"></a>name components:</p>

  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo38;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    given name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo38;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
    additional name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo38;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
    family name
  </p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_d8f979ce-3095-460c-bff0-279a36d008c4" id="_d8f979ce-3095-460c-bff0-279a36d008c4"></a>Vietnamese personal names are names used by those from Vietnam and the
Vietnamese diaspora overseas.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_f8ab322c-4426-4b20-929e-6218daefe42d" id="_f8ab322c-4426-4b20-929e-6218daefe42d"></a>Vietnamese names consist of a family name (T&#xEA;n, &#x20E1B;),
followed by a given name (H&#x1ECD;, /&#x22A5C;).
Between the family name and given name,
one or more additional names may be present.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_084fbaaa-7132-4170-a8ba-e4a128fda10d" id="_084fbaaa-7132-4170-a8ba-e4a128fda10d"></a>Vietnamese additional names can be a
middle name (t&#xEA;n &#x111;&#x1EC7;m),
generational name,
or clan distinguisher name. The middle name, for identification purposes, can be omitted.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_f1259f4b-ab5d-40fa-800b-884ef4a79dfd" id="_f1259f4b-ab5d-40fa-800b-884ef4a79dfd"></a>Courtesy names are also allowed, separate from the given name.</p>
